    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n83371" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῐτῡρ-ίς</span></b>  (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλαία</span>), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>small</i> kind of <i>olive</i>, of the colour of bran,
			which was gathered before it was ripe, and then preserved, acc. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πίτυριν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					50
				</span></i>
			, cf. Philem.Gloss. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				2.56c
			</span></i>. [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῡ</span> prop., but
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ</span> in Call.l.c.]</div>
